		<node type="event_merge" id="9" tag="branch" />
		<node type="event_simple" id="10" tag="">
			<journal_entry>Now that you interacted with $[Resource.C.r_clan_shipyard_NameSingular], double-click on the $[Skill.S.s_shipbuilding_NameSingular] icon, and find the  recipe icon. Double-click on the $[Resource.F.r_figurine_ship_launch_NameSingular] and check the required materials list. In some cases, you may need to scroll down the list. Once you have the required materials in your backpack, select to craft one item and click on the large checkmark. In case the crafting fails, you might need to try again - in this case you will need some more materials again.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="interact_with_object" id="0" value="1" tag="An Interact With Object Task" resource_name="r_Clan Shipyard">
					<task_instruction>Find and Interact with $[Resource.C.r_clan_shipyard_NameSingular]</task_instruction>
				</task>
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="11" tag="">
			<journal_entry>Now that you have crafted the $[Resource.F.r_figurine_ship_launch_NameSingular] it should have been placed in your backpack. If you are near a large body of water, double-click on the figurine to use it while aiming at the water. You will then need to climb aboard and interact with the helm to start sailing.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="craft_item" id="1" value="1" tag="A Craft Item(s) Task" resource_name="r_Figurine Ship Launch" quantity="1">
					<task_instruction>Construct a $[Resource.S.r_ship_launch_NameSingular]</task_instruction>
				</task>
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="12" tag="">
			<journal_entry>To sail, press and hold the Forward run key. The ship will start to pick up speed. You can turn as if you would when controlling your character. Pressing the Spacebar will raise any fishing nets that are available to prevent boarders from climbing aboard. You can repair damaged ships when not at the helm using $[Resource.R.r_repair_shard_NamePlural]. When in a Safe Zone, there is a cooldown duration to when someone else can take control of the ship&apos;s helm. This is not true when not in a safe zone.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="activate_item" id="2" value="1" tag="An Activate Item Task" resource_name="r_Figurine Ship Launch" consume="False">
					<task_instruction>Spawn a $[Resource.S.r_ship_launch_NameSingular]</task_instruction>
				</task>
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="end_node" id="13" tag="">
